# Handlers

This page is the application-layer guide for HTTP updates. The contract is
[Runtime](/docs/reference/runtime/) and
[Server](/docs/reference/language/server/).

Counter increment patches `#counter`. A command returns empty SSE to Datastar
and 204 otherwise.

Spell every route as `@method:role(path)`. Role-first forms are **removed**.

Rocci treats HTML as the shared boundary. Datastar sends intent and morphs
HTML. It is not a client application framework and not a Rocci language
feature. Durable state stays on the server.

## Choose a shape

| Goal | Declaration | Browser result |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Full page | `@get:view("path")` | Document load or navigate |
| Read an HTML fragment | `@get:fragment("path")` | Finite `datastar-patch-elements` |
| Replace HTML after a mutation | `@post:fragment("path")` | Finite `datastar-patch-elements` |
| Perform a write, no representation | `@post:command("path")` | Empty SSE to Datastar; 204 otherwise |
| Stream shared HTML | `@get:live("path")` | Long-lived SSE at that path |

There is no default method. Mutation fragments and commands also allow
`@put`, `@patch`, and `@delete`. Live paths are plural; use one coherence
stream when possible. Do not morph the same `id` from both a finite fragment
and a live stream.

Canonical one-shot: [Counter](/examples/counter/).
Canonical stream: [Live counter](/examples/live-counter/).
Advanced standalone game: [Rocci Blocks](/examples/blocks/).
Complete matrix: [Handler matrix](/examples/handler-matrix/).

## Wire the button

```rocci
<button data-on:click=@post("/actions/inc")>Inc</button>
```

`@post("/path")` is a Rocci action (Roc string, double quotes). A quoted
`"@post('…')"` is opaque Datastar JS. For row-specific URLs, make the
attribute a Roc expression.

Commands return `{}` and carry no success representation. Generated commands
are empty SSE for Datastar and 204 otherwise.

## Request, errors, logging

Generated dispatch calls `handler!(context, request)`. List `request` when you
read the body, headers, or route data. Keep `?` at the effectful edge. A
failing handler returns HTTP 500. `rocci run --log-handlers` prints the
matched route. Log with `Stderr.line!` from handlers, never from `@component`.

**Related:** [Standalone](/docs/applications/standalone/),
[Attributes](/docs/reference/language/attributes/).
